open-trofeo-lcd (0.1.0~dev20260520+resolute7) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Development preview package for Ubuntu testing.
  * Repair theme-library path validation so a theme entry is fixed when its
    path points at a different theme document with a matching existing file.
  * Keep all animation assets referenced by the six bundled starter themes.
  * Add explicit AppStream package mapping so Discover can associate the
    open-trofeo-lcd DEB update with its application metadata.
  * Re-render and resend the active LCD theme when brightness changes, so the
    Configuration brightness control has a visible effect on the display.
  * Add Theme Designer auto-arrange for selected layers or all visible widgets
    and stats, with layout buckets for media, weather, forecast, gauges,
    progress, sparklines and EQ.
  * Use a lowercase AppStream/Desktop ID so Discover can associate the DEB
    package with app metadata, author, license and screenshots.
  * Expand AppStream metadata with clearer native-package access details.
  * Restore reliable animated-theme LCD output by keeping live overlays in
    full 1920x462 canvas coordinates instead of using rotated crop boxes.
  * Prevent stale Theme Designer preview renders from snapping dragged
    elements back visually after release.
  * Refresh and align the six bundled starter themes with safer left/top
    margins and more consistent media, weather, EQ and telemetry placement.
  * Add TRCC USB recovery helper for post-suspend and timeout startup paths.
  * Install six polished starter themes and refreshed previews.
  * Depend on CAVA/OpenCV/Numpy for the current EQ and animation workflows.
  * Keep TRCC as an optional acceleration path; use native PyUSB by default.
  * Refresh AppStream metadata, Discover screenshots and package icon wiring.
  * Build binary packages with root-owned payload files.
  * Allow the packaged backend to start without the legacy Windows PCAP file.
  * Bundle the captured Trofeo LCD packet template used by the stable native
    transfer path.
  * Install user systemd templates in the DEB and make packaged backend service
    launches go through /usr/bin/open-trofeo-lcd so the workdir is refreshed
    after package upgrades.
  * Install and globally enable the packaged user backend service unit.
  * Report real package version in the UI.

